# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 5 — User Capabilities

---

# Purpose

This section defines every capability available within DigiSwasthya.

A capability describes something a user should be able to accomplish.

Capabilities define the product.

They do not define user interface, implementation, workflows, or technical architecture.

Every feature, page, button, API, and workflow exists only to support one or more capabilities defined in this document.

If the application cannot perform a capability described here, the application is incomplete.

If the application performs actions not described here, the product definition should be updated before implementation.

---

# Capability Principles

Every capability should satisfy the following principles.

- Solve a real business problem.
- Produce a measurable business outcome.
- Belong to one or more user roles.
- Follow business rules.
- Preserve data integrity.
- Leave an audit trail where applicable.
- Integrate with existing business entities.
- Never duplicate another capability.

---

# Capability Structure

Every capability should define:

- Purpose
- Applicable User Roles
- Business Outcome
- Dependencies
- Restrictions
- Success Criteria

Implementation details are intentionally excluded.

